  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Foreign in Two Homelands (2024), published by Cambridge University Press, has been cited 8 times. Beyond that, it is used in teaching and has been written about in The Conversation.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Foreign in Two Homelands by Michelle Lynn Kahn was published by Cambridge University Press in 2024. It is part of the Publications of the German Historical Institute series. Conceptually, the work connects to Political science and History. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) \u2014 History.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 8 citations. Citations peaked in 2026 with 4 citing works. Notable citing venues include The History of the Family, New German Critique and Rethinking History. They come from 6 countries, led by the United States, Germany and the United Kingdom.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture. It has also been written about for a general audience in The Conversation.</p>",
